add(31,'Adi Parva',1,'Adhyaya 214-220 (Khandava narrative)','Khandava Forest Episode',['Krishna','Arjuna','Agni'],'Agni seeks assistance to consume the Khandava forest and Krishna and Arjuna agree to help, obtaining the means needed for the task.','Meeting a difficult objective while facing powerful external interference and resource constraints.','Krishna and Arjuna secure suitable weapons and coordinate their roles to protect Agni while the objective is pursued.','The requested objective is accomplished after sustained coordinated effort.','Strategy / Resource Management','A project team has a difficult objective and must secure the tools and roles needed before execution.','Clarify the objective, secure required capabilities, and coordinate roles before taking on a difficult task.','A team should identify critical dependencies and assign complementary responsibilities before execution.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m01/index.htm')
add(32,'Adi Parva',1,'Adhyaya 182-193 (Swayamvara narrative)','Draupadi Swayamvara',['Arjuna','Draupadi','Drupada'],'The Pandavas, living in disguise, participate in a demanding contest while maintaining their concealed identity.','Demonstrating capability while operating under uncertainty and identity constraints.','Arjuna focuses on the task and succeeds without prematurely exposing the group.','The Pandavas gain a major alliance through the outcome.','Decision Making / Alliance','A small team needs to demonstrate capability publicly while protecting sensitive information.','Focus on the objective while controlling unnecessary exposure of sensitive information.','Reveal only information necessary for the decision while allowing demonstrated capability to establish credibility.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m01/index.htm')
add(33,'Sabha Parva',2,'Dice-game sections','The Dice Game and Loss of the Kingdom',['Yudhishthira','Shakuni','Duryodhana'],'Yudhishthira accepts a sequence of wagers in a hostile setting and progressively loses control of the situation.','Recognizing escalating risk and the danger of continuing after adverse outcomes.','Yudhishthira continues participating despite worsening losses.','The Pandavas lose wealth, kingdom and freedom in the sequence of wagers.','Risk / Decision Making','A person or team keeps increasing commitment after repeated losses because of pressure or sunk costs.','A deteriorating decision environment should trigger reassessment rather than automatic continuation.','Set stop conditions and reassess after major losses instead of escalating commitment solely to recover previous losses.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m02/index.htm')
add(34,'Sabha Parva',2,'Dice-game and assembly sections','Draupadi in the Kuru Assembly',['Draupadi','Yudhishthira','Bhishma','Vidura','Duryodhana'],'Draupadi challenges the legitimacy of her treatment in the assembly and asks questions about rights and responsibility.','Handling a contested decision where authority, procedure and legitimacy are disputed.','Draupadi publicly questions the legal and ethical basis of the action.','The assembly fails to resolve the dispute cleanly, and the conflict deepens.','Ethics / Governance','An organization faces a contested decision and stakeholders question whether the process was legitimate.','When legitimacy is disputed, examine the decision process and responsibilities rather than relying only on authority.','Create a transparent review process and document the basis for contested decisions.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m02/index.htm')
add(35,'Vana Parva',3,'Yaksha-prashna sections','Yaksha Prashna',['Yudhishthira','Yaksha'],'Yudhishthira faces a sequence of difficult questions under pressure after his brothers have fallen unconscious.','Making careful decisions when information is limited and the consequences of error are high.','Yudhishthira listens, answers carefully, and prioritizes judgment rather than rushing.','He answers successfully and his brothers are restored.','Uncertainty / Decision Making','A project lead must make a high-consequence decision with incomplete information and limited time.','Under uncertainty, deliberate reasoning and attention to the decision constraints can outperform impulsive action.','Identify the critical unknowns, evaluate options carefully, and avoid rushing solely because others are pressuring the decision.','https://original.sacred-texts.com/hin/m03/index.htm')
add(36,'Vana Parva',3,'Adhyaya 12-24 (Kirmira narrative)','Kirmira Encounter',['Bhima','Kirmira','Yudhishthira'],'The Pandavas encounter a hostile threat during exile and must protect their group while continuing their journey.','Protecting a team while maintaining progress during an unexpected disruption.','Bhima confronts the immediate threat while the rest of the group remains protected.','The threat is defeated and the group continues.','Crisis Management','A team encounters an unexpected disruptive threat while operating away from normal support.','Separate immediate threat handling from the broader mission so the whole team is not exposed unnecessarily.','Assign a capable response role while preserving the continuity of the main operation.','https://original.sacred-texts.com/hin/m03/index.htm')
add(37,'Vana Parva',3,'Adhyaya 233-233 (Draupadi-Satyabhama Samvada)','Draupadi and Satyabhama Dialogue',['Draupadi','Satyabhama'],'Satyabhama asks Draupadi about maintaining relationships and household responsibilities under difficult circumstances.','Managing relationships and responsibilities consistently despite demanding circumstances.','Draupadi describes disciplined routines, responsibilities and conduct.','The dialogue presents a model of sustained responsibility and relationship management.','Leadership / Communication','A team leader must maintain trust and responsibilities during a stressful project period.','Consistency in responsibilities and communication helps preserve trust during pressure.','Set clear responsibilities and maintain predictable communication during demanding periods.','https://original.sacred-texts.com/hin/m03/index.htm')
add(38,'Virata Parva',4,'Kichaka-badha Parva, Sections XIV-XXV','Kichaka Incident',['Draupadi','Bhima','Kichaka'],'Draupadi faces harassment by a powerful court figure while the Pandavas must preserve their disguise.','Addressing a serious internal threat without exposing a larger strategic position.','Bhima and Draupadi arrange a controlled confrontation that removes the immediate threat while preserving the disguise.','Kichaka is killed and the Pandavas remain undiscovered.','Crisis Management / Risk','A team faces a serious internal threat while disclosure of its wider operation would create additional risk.','Resolve the immediate threat while protecting the confidentiality of the broader mission.','Use controlled escalation and limit unnecessary disclosure when the surrounding operation is sensitive.','https://original.sacred-texts.com/hin/m04/index.htm')
add(39,'Virata Parva',4,'Go-harana Parva, Sections XXVI-LXXII','Recovery of Virata’s Cattle',['Arjuna','Uttara','Virata','Kaurava army'],'The Kaurava forces seize Virata’s cattle and Uttara initially lacks confidence to confront the threat.','Recovering critical assets when the available leader or team initially lacks confidence.','Arjuna takes the operational lead while Uttara serves in a supporting role.','The cattle are recovered and the opposing force is repelled.','Leadership / Resource Management','A team must recover critical assets when its nominal lead is inexperienced or overwhelmed.','Match roles to capability and allow experienced members to take the critical operational role.','Reassign responsibilities according to competence rather than rigidly following nominal hierarchy.','https://original.sacred-texts.com/hin/m04/index.htm')
add(40,'Udyoga Parva',5,'Sections XXXI-XL','Sanjaya’s Peace Mission',['Sanjaya','Yudhishthira','Krishna','Duryodhana'],'Sanjaya carries messages between the opposing sides while both parties assess whether peace remains possible.','Communicating between parties with incompatible interests without escalating the conflict.','Sanjaya presents the position of one side while seeking a peaceful resolution.','The exchange clarifies positions but does not prevent the later escalation.','Diplomacy / Communication','A mediator must communicate between two groups with strong disagreements.','A mediator should accurately communicate positions while preserving room for peaceful settlement.','Separate factual communication from inflammatory language and identify points where compromise remains possible.','https://original.sacred-texts.com/hin/m05/index.htm')
add(41,'Udyoga Parva',5,'Sanat-sujata Parva, Sections XLI-LXXI','Vidura and Sanat-sujata Counsel',['Vidura','Dhritarashtra','Sanat-sujata'],'Dhritarashtra seeks counsel about difficult matters, and Vidura brings in Sanat-sujata to address deeper doubts.','Seeking appropriate expertise when existing advice is insufficient.','Vidura recognizes the limits of his own role and introduces another source of counsel.','Dhritarashtra receives additional counsel addressing his doubts.','Leadership / Knowledge Management','A leader encounters a problem beyond the expertise of the immediate team.','Good decision-making includes recognizing when to seek specialized expertise.','Escalate to a qualified specialist when the existing decision group lacks the required knowledge.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m05/index.htm')
add(42,'Udyoga Parva',5,'Sections XXIV-XXXI','Vidura’s Counsel and the Cost of Ignoring Advice',['Vidura','Dhritarashtra','Duryodhana'],'Wise counsel repeatedly warns against policies that increase internal conflict, but the advice is not followed.','Handling decision-making when leaders receive credible but inconvenient advice.','Vidura gives warnings while the leadership continues to favor other counsel.','The conflict worsens and the consequences become harder to avoid.','Governance / Decision Making','A leadership team repeatedly ignores credible internal warnings because they conflict with preferred plans.','Decision quality suffers when credible dissent is systematically excluded.','Create a formal process for recording and evaluating dissenting expert opinions before major decisions.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m05/index.htm')
add(43,'Bhishma Parva',6,'Bhagavad-Gita Parva, Sections XXV-XLII','Arjuna’s Crisis and the Bhagavad Gita',['Arjuna','Krishna'],'Arjuna becomes unable to act because the decision carries severe personal and moral consequences.','Making a difficult decision when competing duties and emotional pressures conflict.','Krishna helps Arjuna examine duty, action, knowledge and consequences before acting.','Arjuna regains clarity and proceeds with the required action.','Ethics / Decision Making','A person faces a difficult professional decision where personal concerns conflict with role responsibilities.','Structured reflection on duties, consequences and values can reduce decision paralysis.','Separate emotional reaction from explicit responsibilities and evaluate the decision against stated values and role obligations.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m06/index.htm')
add(44,'Bhishma Parva',6,'Bhishma’s fall sections','The Fall of Bhishma',['Bhishma','Arjuna','Shikhandi','Krishna'],'The Pandavas face an opponent whose strength makes direct neutralization difficult.','Finding a viable strategy against a highly capable opponent without relying on brute force alone.','The Pandavas use Shikhandi in the battle plan because of Bhishma’s stated constraints.','Bhishma is brought down from the field.','Strategy / Constraint Management','A project faces a competitor or obstacle whose strengths make direct competition inefficient.','Effective strategy can exploit constraints and choose a favorable interaction rather than confronting maximum strength directly.','Map the constraints of the problem and select an approach that reduces the opponent’s strongest advantage.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m06/index.htm')
add(45,'Drona Parva',7,'Abhimanyu-badha Parva, Sections XXXI-XL','Abhimanyu and the Chakravyuha',['Abhimanyu','Arjuna','Drona','Jayadratha'],'Abhimanyu enters a complex formation with incomplete knowledge of how to exit it while the opposing side restricts support.','Making a decision under incomplete information and asymmetric access to support.','Abhimanyu commits to the objective despite incomplete knowledge of the full maneuver.','He becomes isolated and is ultimately killed after being surrounded.','Uncertainty / Strategy','A team enters a complex project with incomplete knowledge and limited access to support.','Before entering a complex environment, verify both entry and exit conditions and identify support dependencies.','Define exit criteria, escalation paths and support requirements before committing to a complex task.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m07/index.htm')
add(46,'Drona Parva',7,'Dronabhisheka and Drona-vadha sections','Drona’s Command and Neutralization',['Drona','Krishna','Yudhishthira','Ashwatthaman'],'Drona’s battlefield capability makes him difficult to stop directly, and the opposing side searches for another way to change the situation.','Responding to a highly capable adversary whose direct neutralization is difficult.','The Pandavas use information about Ashwatthaman to affect Drona’s willingness to continue fighting.','Drona lays down his weapons and is killed.','Strategy / Information','A team faces an opponent whose direct capability is difficult to counter.','Information can alter strategic behavior, but its use requires careful consideration of accuracy and ethics.','Use verified information and evaluate ethical and reputational consequences before relying on information asymmetry.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m07/index.htm')
add(47,'Karna Parva',8,'Arjuna-Karna battle sections','Arjuna and Karna’s Final Duel',['Arjuna','Karna','Krishna','Shalya'],'The two principal warriors face a decisive confrontation while equipment, terrain and timing affect the encounter.','Managing a high-stakes decision under changing operational constraints.','Krishna responds to changing battlefield conditions while Arjuna maintains focus on the objective.','Karna is defeated in the final confrontation.','Decision Making / Risk','A team faces a high-stakes decision where conditions can change during execution.','Monitor changing constraints during execution rather than treating the original plan as fixed.','Use real-time checkpoints and contingency decisions for high-stakes operations.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m08/index.htm')
add(48,'Shalya Parva',9,'Final battle sections','Bhima and Duryodhana’s Mace Duel',['Bhima','Duryodhana','Krishna','Balarama'],'The final duel is governed by known rules and both opponents have different strengths.','Competing under explicit constraints while adapting to an opponent’s strengths.','Bhima and Krishna account for Duryodhana’s physical advantage and the rules of the duel.','Bhima defeats Duryodhana.','Strategy / Constraint Management','Two teams compete under fixed rules while each has different strengths.','A strategy should account for both formal constraints and the opponent’s strongest capability.','Identify the rules that cannot be changed and design tactics around the opponent’s strengths and weaknesses.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m09/index.htm')
add(49,'Sauptika Parva',10,'Sections I-IX','Ashvatthama’s Night Attack',['Ashvatthama','Kripa','Kritavarman'],'After the main battle, Ashvatthama chooses a night attack against a vulnerable camp.','Deciding whether to act immediately after a major conflict when the target is vulnerable but the action carries severe consequences.','Ashvatthama chooses a surprise night attack rather than waiting.','The attack causes extensive destruction and creates further consequences.','Risk / Ethics','A team can exploit a temporary vulnerability but must consider long-term consequences and legitimacy.','Short-term tactical advantage can create severe long-term costs when ethical and reputational consequences are ignored.','Evaluate second-order effects and legitimacy before exploiting a temporary advantage.','https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m10/index.htm')
